    "body": "> [...] specificity for these pseudo-classes [...]\r\n\r\nThe spec states: https://drafts.csswg.org/selectors-5/#headings\r\n\r\n> The [specificity](https://drafts.csswg.org/selectors-4/#specificity) of [:heading()](https://drafts.csswg.org/selectors-5/#heading-functional-pseudo) is that of a class.\r\n\r\nThis was updated in https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/pull/12404 which while not updated in April as claimed, was updated today!\r\n\r\nAIUI this is per the resolution in https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10296#issuecomment-2775988542.\r\n\r\n> RESOLVED: `:heading()` has the expected class-level specificity",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/3014280728/reactions",
